    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7624",
      "problem": "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x).$ Plot the graph of $y=2f\\left(3(x+3)\\right)+5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/b314de8320a82ad5a7bd395da63c6f9bd4348ee2f4fd12c13a090c20fbcdd322.png)",
      "worked_solution": "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f.$ We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot $y=2f\\left({3}(x+3)\\right)+5,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x).$\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left({3}x\\right).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/92ffae3729220d6eae6cfb96fde2efc93f19b58ad38a5ba36760fb8b38ee8ced.png)\n\n- Then, translate it left by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=f\\left({3}(x+3)\\right).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/c4fc767f318d276a0178f4ceb2d2550a5141744ca2c3ed8da1f240309d3a1ca0.png)\n\n- Then, stretch it by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=2f\\left(3(x+3)\\right).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/143a49c724c30a9e9cf432960fcf7046784a9a881182959875b9805adb0a8c5e.png)\n\n- Finally, translate it up by $5$ units to get the graph of $y=2f\\left(3(x+3)\\right)+5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/assets/6d7295138c2821d0d3c479ff9d98e2018bc26493ff09f41fe463cc31cee0907e.png)",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14215685/observations/step-e7624-39117b976c8324131564.html",
      "source_url": "https://mathacademy.com/tasks/14215685/topics/634/lesson",
